# Webhook Returns <%= edit_link %>

Webhook Returns allows Skroutz Merchants to automatically receive return details to their
platform when a new return is created or an existing one is updated (its state or logistics
change), so the merchant's own system can stay in sync without polling the [Returns API](/smart_cart/returns_api).

> <i class="fa fa-exclamation-triangle"></i>
> Webhook Returns is currently **under development** .

> When a return's `state` is `pending_merchant_review`, the payload also includes a
> `review_options` list describing what the merchant can do next — see
> [Review options](/smart_cart/returns_api#review-options).

> When a return's `state` is `pending_service_inspection`, the payload also includes a
> `service_request` object describing what the merchant can currently submit — see
> [Service status](/smart_cart/returns_api#service-status).

<%= partial 'partials/toc' %>

## Setup

In order to be able to use the webhook, a **return webhook URL** should be registered
by the merchant from within
[Smart Cart settings](https://<%= settings.merchants_domain %>/merchants/account/shop/ecommerce_details)
page in merchant's panel (Merchants > Services > [Skroutz Marketplace](https://<%= settings.merchants_domain %>/merchants/account/shop/ecommerce_details)).

> <i class="fa fa-exclamation-triangle"></i>
> Registering a URL alone does not enable delivery — the **return webhook** must also be
> explicitly turned on from the same settings page. Both are required before any request is sent.

Webhook Returns requests are sent from the same infrastructure as
[Webhook Orders](/smart_cart/orders_webhook#setup) requests, so the same IP ranges apply:

<%= partial 'partials/webhook_ip_ranges' %>

> <i class="fa fa-exclamation-triangle"></i>
> The **webhook URL should match the shop's domain** and it should follow secure **HTTP (HTTPS)**

##### Webhook URL example

Shop URL | Webhook URL
-------- | ----------
`https://shop.gr` | `https://shop.gr/smart_cart_returns`

## Webhook requests

An HTTP `POST` request is sent to the predefined return webhook URL once an event has been triggered.

### The anatomy of a request

##### Request
<pre class="terminal">
POST {webhook_url}
</pre>

##### Request headers

Header         | Value
-------------- | -----
`Content-Type` | `application/json; charset=utf-8`
`User-Agent`   | `Skroutz OrderNotifier v1` (shared with [Webhook Orders](/smart_cart/orders_webhook#the-anatomy-of-a-request))

> <i class="fa fa-exclamation-triangle"></i>
> Since the `User-Agent` value is shared with [Webhook Orders](/smart_cart/orders_webhook), it cannot
> be used to distinguish order from return notifications. Use the `event_type` field in the request
> body instead.

##### Expected request response

<pre class="terminal">
200
</pre>

## Webhook events

The available webhook events for which a request is performed are:

* **return created** events
* **return updated** events

### Return created

A **return created** webhook request (`merchant_return_created`) is triggered once, right after a
return is first placed. If the return needs the merchant's own judgment before Skroutz can
proceed, it's created directly in the `pending_merchant_review` state and the payload's `return`
object carries a `review_options` list — see [Example 1](#example-1-return-created) and
[Review options](/smart_cart/returns_api#review-options).

### Return updated

A **return updated** webhook request (`merchant_return_updated`) is triggered whenever:

* The return's **state changes** (e.g. escalated to `pending_merchant_review`, approved by the
  merchant, marked as returning, returned, rejected, expired or cancelled). If the update moves
  the return into `pending_merchant_review`, the payload's `return` object additionally carries a
  `review_options` list — see [Example 6](#example-6-return-updated---escalated-to-merchant-review).
  If the update instead moves the return into `pending_service_inspection`, the payload's `return`
  object additionally carries a `service_request` object instead — see
  [Example 7](#example-7-return-updated---needs-service-inspection). If the update instead makes
  shipment information newly available — for example when the return transitions into the
  `returning` state — the payload additionally carries the `courier` and `returning_address`
  fields.
* The return's **courier is reassigned** on an existing return shipment.
* The return's **courier tracking IDs become available**.

> <i class="fa fa-exclamation-triangle"></i>
> A **return updated** request is only sent once a **return created** request has already been
> delivered for that same return and webhook URL. In practice, if you enable the return webhook
> (or change its URL) *after* a return already exists, that return will not receive update events
> until a fresh **return created** event has been recorded against the new URL.

#### Request payload

Name         | Type   | Value | Description
------------ | ------ | ----- | ------------------
`event_type` | String | `merchant_return_created`, `merchant_return_updated` | Return event type
`event_time` | Date String in format<br> `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ` | | Event creation time
`return`     | Object |  | [Return details](#return-object)
`changes`    | Object |  | [Return changes with old and new values (optional)](#return-changes-object)

<%= partial 'localizable/smart_cart/return_object' %>

#### Return changes object

Only present on **return updated** requests, and only includes the keys that actually changed.

Field                  | Shape          | Notes
----------------------- | -------------- | -----
`state`                | `{ old, new }` | Raw state values, see [return object](#return-object)
`courier`              | `{ old, new }` | Human-readable courier name; `old` can be `null` when courier info first becomes available
`returning_address`    | `{ old, new }` | Same shape as [returning address](#returning-address)
`courier_tracking_ids` | `{ old, new }` | Only included when a `new` value is actually present

> `review_options` and `service_request` are not tracked in `changes` — their disappearance is
> implied by the `state` change off `pending_merchant_review` / `pending_service_inspection` (see
> [Review options](/smart_cart/returns_api#review-options) and
> [Service status](/smart_cart/returns_api#service-status)).

## Payload Examples

#### Example 1 (return created)

~~~ json
{
  "event_type": "merchant_return_created",
  "event_time": "2026-08-18T09:12:03Z",
  "return": {
    "return_code": "R-111111-1111111",
    "state": "pending_merchant_review",
    "order_code": "48213907",
    "created_at": "2026-08-18T09:12:03Z",
    "return_line_items": [
      {
        "id": "gY6oNzr8jp",
        "ean": "1234567890123",
        "product_name": "Apple iPhone 15 128GB",
        "returning_quantity": 1,
        "return_reason": "wrong_product",
        "user_comment": "Ordered black, received white.",
        "user_photos": [
          "https://api.skroutz.gr/assets/returns/photo_1.jpg"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "review_options": [
      { "option": "approve" },
      { "option": "resolved_via_customer_communication", "comment_required": false, "supports_proposed_part_url_required": false },
      { "option": "incorrect_skroutz_content", "comment_required": true, "supports_proposed_part_url_required": false }
    ]
  }
}
~~~

#### Example 2 (return updated - shipment info newly available)

~~~ json
{
  "event_type": "merchant_return_updated",
  "event_time": "2026-08-19T10:00:00Z",
  "return": {
    "return_code": "R-111111-1111111",
    "state": "returning",
    "order_code": "48213907",
    "created_at": "2026-08-18T09:12:03Z",
    "courier": "ACS",
    "returning_address": {
      "street_name": "Ermou",
      "street_number": "12",
      "zip": "10563",
      "city": "Athens",
      "region": "Attica",
      "country_code": "GR"
    },
    "return_line_items": [
      { "id": "gY6oNzr8jp", "ean": "1234567890123", "product_name": "Apple iPhone 15 128GB", "returning_quantity": 1 }
    ]
  },
  "changes": {
    "state": { "old": "pending_merchant_review", "new": "returning" },
    "courier": { "old": null, "new": "ACS" },
    "returning_address": {
      "old": null,
      "new": {
        "street_name": "Ermou",
        "street_number": "12",
        "zip": "10563",
        "city": "Athens",
        "region": "Attica",
        "country_code": "GR"
      }
    }
  }
}
~~~

